{"claims":[{"claim_text":"The greatest threat to the security of the Afghan people and the American people lies in the tribal regions of Pakistan, where terrorists train, plot attacks, and strike into Afghanistan and move back across the border.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"A sanctuary for Al Qaeda cannot be tolerated.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"A stronger and sustained partnership between Afghanistan, Pakistan, and NATO is needed, including necessary assets like satellites and predator drones, to better secure the border, to take out terrorist camps, and to crack down on cross-border insurgents.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Pakistan needs help to develop its own counter-terrorism and counter-insurgency capacity.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Investment in the long-term development of the Pashtun border region will meet the extremists' program of hate with an agenda of hope.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"More will be asked of the Pakistani government, rather than offering a blank check to an undemocratic President.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Non-military aid to the Pakistani people will be significantly increased and sustained for a decade.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Military assistance provided to Pakistan will be ensured to be used to fight extremists.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"An alliance with Pakistan should move beyond being built on individual leaders to avoid mounting opposition in a nuclear-armed nation at the nexus of terror, extremism, and instability wrought by autocracy.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

